  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As everybody knows at this point the Valve Knuckles are one of the best VR Controllers on the market due to Valve's implementation of finger tracking. Finger tracking for VRChat is both a blessing and a curse. A blessing because of individual finger positioning, and a curse for those who want to use simple gesture toggles for props and even meme avatars. For instance say I had rock and roll as a gesture toggle that spawns a soda can, on the HTC wands and Oculus controllers I could have my hand look like as though I am holding a can, but because the knuckles override the hand gesture layer, if I assign the command for the soda can to rock and roll, my hand in game would also be doing the rock and roll gesture. Would it be possible to disable finger tracking and enable easy gestures similar to the Oculus hand gesture commands?",
